{"title":"1991 AHSME Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409af0b9d79fd0611cc939af87e1cc1fe08ba3ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{10}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> is rotated <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> counter-clockwise about the origin to obtain a new graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/4266c984c216eb19c23f8c0bfc87639017930763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Which of the following is an equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/6/4266c984c216eb19c23f8c0bfc87639017930763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p>(A) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bf07b1ea740b8f194730ef49687db8521f703a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{10}\\left(\\frac{x+90}{9}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"151\" height=\"43\" /> (B) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3a1f150b03ab3b9f7fb21e3643f95e25011661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{x}10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> (C) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583c5ef513fb705e2751dda514a27979d8a05ddc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{1}{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"78\" height=\"38\" /> (D) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/38616ba7eac537b0a02c89069e5f137a94665fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10^{-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" /> (E) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8ea44969a9dd7e814ef1142f55a896770d1877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/25809e4f87f20a2ee949878bc603b9eda09422ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> Rotating a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> anticlockwise about the origin maps it to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4137c571b8f36631228bbcd177712f85c41e9176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-y,x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> (You can prove this geometrically, or using matrices if you aren't convinced). Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41b509a8fee5727b8a25300df46a1e3f68e3eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, \\log_{10}x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> maps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655eec66da8d587a01e80964d5676037bc1d42cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\log_{10}x, x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, so new <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/a/32a5a247b9b33fe97b482e31bdc5e5147134ac96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> old <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/6/9363eaeea043e0d7ccbaba342321cef3920b6b2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 10^{\\log_{10}x} = 10^{-(-\\log_{10}x)} = 10^{-\\text{new} x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"291\" height=\"16\" />, so the new equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/88449701a16926c8f241ab72a1ccb2e97b91d306.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=10^{-x}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME\" title=\"1991 AHSME\">1991 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1991 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</